Z||000000||delSol97||11-25-2001||07:10 AM||||I've found bits and pieces, but I'm looking for a decent FAQ or buildguide for doing a convertible.<P>I want to show my welder exactly where I want tubing welded.<P>I like the X-frame idea but I want something that still makes gas tank, tranny, etc access easy.<P>Any ideas where to look?<P>Pics would be great.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||fieroparts.com||11-25-2001||10:10 AM|||| This X frame will let you drop your tank<BR>WITHOUT removing the X frame. The center unbolts so you can get to the tank.<P> <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=598358809" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=598358809</A>  <P>||||reg||14
Z||000002||Oreif||11-25-2001||11:53 AM||||E-mail Bob Steiger at Twin Lakes Fiero, He runs his bracing thru the frame rails and welds them to the strut/shock towers. He has done a few convertables this way. One even has a 3800SC engine in the back and there is no sagging or twisting. A Forum member named Coyote also did it this way. If you E-mail him he can probably send you detailed pic's of his chassis and explain in detail how he did it. (he did it the same way Bob does) He is making a Speedster version of a Fiero and was also planning on dropping in a V-8.||||reg||1
